>are there any reasons not to do this? 

  You have to be able to get to Expert in dagger.  It costs 6 skill slots.
Only Rangers, Rogues, Tourists, Valkyries, and Wizards can get to Expert in
dagger.  (Other roles can get to Expert in other multi-shot missile
weapons.)

  If you like 2x for Expert, Rangers and Rogues get a class bonus of an
additional dagger chance per fling, averaging 2.5x at Expert.


  Rogues start with some daggers and basic skill.  The Rogue backstab bonus
gets multiplied too.  Something like XL/2 per hit on a scared monster.  At
XL:10 that's an additional 2.5 x 5 = 12.5 all by itself.  Use Elbereth, a
horn, or a drum and fire away.  

  Someone on #nethack asked "Isn't that a bit exploitish?"  Exploitish is
what being a Rogue is all about.

  So if you want a whole new experience in NetHack, play a Rogue and throw
daggers early and often.  Since you hate pets they look like the way to go.


  Scare monsters with the spell, Elbereth, horn, drum, etc.  Throwing +7
Expert daggers at XL:14 will average 56 points of damage per fling against
a scared monster.  (Aligned temples become killing grounds.)

  Rogues LOSE the backstab bonus when twoweaponing.

